      "solve": {
        "summary": "A charge placed at the center of a face of a cube contributes half of its flux to the cube: \\(\\Phi_1 = \\frac{1}{2} \\frac{q/2}{\\varepsilon_0} = \\frac{q}{4\\varepsilon_0}\\). A charge placed at a corner of a cube contributes one-eighth of its flux to the cube: \\(\\Phi_2 = \\frac{1}{8} \\frac{2q}{\\varepsilon_0} = \\frac{q}{4\\varepsilon_0}\\). The total flux through the cube is \\(\\Phi = \\Phi_1 + \\Phi_2 = \\frac{q}{2\\varepsilon_0}\\). Comparing this with the given expression \\(\\frac{nq}{2\\varepsilon_0}\\), we find \\(n = 1\\).",
        "answer": "1",
        "uncertainty": "None",
        "figureRequired": false
      },
      "mode": "live"
    },
