      "solve": {
        "summary": "Herbs and shrubs growing under the shade of tall canopy trees (understory plants) receive light that has been filtered through the upper leaves. Since upper canopy leaves selectively absorb red and blue light for photosynthesis, the light reaching the lower strata is relatively enriched in green light, which is less efficiently used for photosynthesis, resulting in a lower rate of photosynthesis compared to sun plants.",
        "answer": "(C)",
        "uncertainty": "None",
        "figureRequired": false
      },
      "mode": "live"
    },
    {
      "questionId": "68dea7c2387eea3d0d95f9bb",
      "sourceVersion": "ecf5123b89c47110b4d53156d42741997902edf89c722dc1060a279b41815b6f",
      "solve": {
        "summary": "The path difference introduced by placing slabs in front of the slits is given by $\\Delta x = (\\mu_1 - 1)t_1 - (\\mu_2 - 1)t_2$. Substituting $\\mu_1 = 1.5, t_1 = 2\\text{ mm}$ and $\\mu_2 = 1.4, t_2 = 1.5\\text{ mm}$, we get $\\Delta x = (1.5 - 1)(2) - (1.4 - 1)(1.5) = 1.0 - 0.6 = 0.4\\text{ mm}$. The shift of central maxima is $\\Delta y = \\frac{D}{d}\\Delta x = \\frac{1000\\text{ mm}}{5\\text{ mm}} \\times 0.4\\text{ mm} = 80\\text{ mm} = 8\\text{ cm}$.",
        "answer": "8",
        "uncertainty": "none",
        "figureRequired": false
      },
      "mode": "live"
    },
    {
